Thanks for your contribution @kizdolf 

Did you try to use our [connectors](https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/react/guide/Connectors.html) and more especially the [`connectHits` connector](https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/react/connectors/connectHits.html)? 

I think you can achieve the behavior you want by using it like this: 

```js
import {connectHits} from 'react-instantsearch/connectors';

<InstantSearch
    appId=""
    apiKey=""
    indexName=""
>
    <CustomHits indexName=""/>
</InstantSearch>;

const CustomHits = connectHits(props => {
  const hits = props.hits.map(hit => <p>{hit.name}</p>);
  return <div>
    <p>Index used is : {props.indexName}</p>
    {hits}
  </div>;
});
```

As you can see the `connectHits` connector has the `hits` props to display hits but you can also forward to it any props you want, so I added the `indexName` one. 

Let me know if this can solve your use case :)
